<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $224.3 mln April 29.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $224.3 mln April 29.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $224.3 million surplus on April 29 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 29</p>
<p>Exports: $433.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $287.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $399.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $321.4 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $224.3 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.729 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.840 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $6.273 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $5.097 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.065 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
